# lab/demo/targets.allow.example - template for the operator-created allowlist.
#
# Copy this file to lab/demo/targets.allow (never commit live target details if
# you do not want them in the repository) and put ONE host per line: the hosts
# you are authorised to send the demo's SQL-injection requests to.
#
# Rules enforced by lab/demo/attack.ps1 and lab/demo/attack.sh:
#   * a loopback target (127.0.0.1, 127.0.0.0/8, ::1, localhost) is always
#     allowed and needs no entry: the local rehearsal never leaves the machine;
#   * any other host is REFUSED before the first request unless the exact
#     hostname appears in lab/demo/targets.allow;
#   * blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored; an inline ' # ...'
#     comment after the host is stripped;
#   * there is no wildcard support: list each hostname explicitly; port and path
#     are taken from --TargetUrl / HDD_ATTACK_TARGET;
#   * the scripts never scan, never try other paths and never touch a host that
#     is not in this file. Only run them against sites you own or operate.
#
# Example (replace with your own authorised target; keep the real file out of git
# if your hostname is sensitive):
# shop.example.com
# staging.example.org
